// Title: Disable PUA Protection on Windows Defender
// Sigma ID: 8ffc5407-52e3-478f-9596-0a7371eafe13
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Austin Songer @austinsonger
// Date: 2021-08-04 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects disabling Windows Defender PUA protection
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.tenforums.com/tutorials/32236-enable-disable-microsoft-defender-pua-protection-windows-10-a.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disabled_pua_protection_on_microsoft_defender.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\PUAProtection" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000000)"
